{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And if he will not redeem.</b> Rabbi Jonah said that it should have been 'ואם לא תגאל' [and if you will not redeem]. And likewise 'ובאשת נעורי אל יבגוד' [and with the wife of your youth let him not deal treacherously]. This is impossible, for יבגוד [let him deal treacherously] returns to the word 'ברוחכם' [in your spirit]. So too its meaning: and if the redeemer will not redeem her, then I know, that there is no redeemer closer than you."], :book :ruth, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "The referent of 'ברוחכם' is to Malachi 2:15-16; Ibn Ezra argues the subject of יבגוד there is Elohim, not the husband, hence masculine singular rather than second person."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ruth -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ruth"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:33.717460566Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}